The soft-glass optical shader, style parameters and color processing are
adapted from HaoZai000/softglass 0.1.1, commit
92c131b967515e7c1186f1644fb544521de85caa (Apache-2.0).
https://github.com/HaoZai000/softglass

Soft-glass integration and progressive title-bar blur reference:
HaoZai000/NexioSchedule (AGPL-3.0).
https://github.com/HaoZai000/NexioSchedule
Adaptations for HyperMusic retain the application's AGPL-3.0 license.

Android common/actual dynamic-color implementations are compiled together.
The original Gaussian components remain the fallback path. HyperMusic adds
an optional soft-glass material at shared toolbar, popup, dialog, sheet and
tab surfaces, without changing public Miuix component signatures.

The newer official miuix-glass, miuix-material and miuix-blur sources supplied
as E:/Code/miuix-main are included under src/main/kotlin/upstream (Apache-2.0).
GlassDropdownPreference, GlassIconDropdownMenu, GlassDropdownPopup,
GlassTransformPopup, GlassIconButton, GlassTabRow and GlassSegmentedTabRow
provide the soft-glass menus, controls and their motion directly.
The newer basic TopAppBar source and CascadingPopupDefaults are also included.

Compatibility adaptations isolate the newer blur package as
top.yukonga.miuix.kmp.glass.backdrop, combine Android expect/actual sources,
provide optional application icon/entry slots, and adapt LayerOutsets to the
Compose version used by this application. Dialog and bottom-sheet surfaces
retain the shared application material adapter rather than the newer official
GlassDialog and GlassBottomSheet wrappers.
